This package is derived from DeFoG (Discrete Flow Matching for Graph Generation):

    Yiming Qin, Manuel Madeira, Dorina Thanou, Pascal Frossard.
    "DeFoG: Discrete Flow Matching for Graph Generation." ICML 2025.
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.04263
    https://github.com/qym7/DeFoG

The base model (graph transformer, noise distributions, rate-matrix construction, time
distortion, RRWP features) follows the upstream implementation, which is MIT licensed
(Copyright (c) 2012-2025 Manuel Madeira, Yiming Qin; see LICENSE). The upstream notice is
retained as required.

Provenance. The code in this package was ported from a research fork of DeFoG (commit
68637b5 of that fork), keeping only the features that have a recorded positive result there.
Features that were tried and failed, came out null, or were never tried are not included.
Frozen-base adapters, Feynman-Kac steering, GDPO reinforcement-learning fine-tuning, learned
size conditioning and the molecular domain code were added in that fork.

Methods used in this package, and the papers they come from (titles and authors as listed on
arXiv):

    DeFoG: Discrete Flow Matching for Graph Generation (base model)
        Qin, Madeira, Thanou, Frossard.                        arXiv:2410.04263
    Discrete Feynman-Kac Correctors (Feynman-Kac / SMC steering)
        Hasan, Ohanesian, Gazizov, Bengio, Aspuru-Guzik,
        Bondesan, Skreta, Neklyudov.                           arXiv:2601.10403
    Graph Diffusion Policy Optimization (GDPO reinforcement-learning fine-tuning)
        Liu, Du, Pang, Li, Lin, Chen.                          arXiv:2402.16302
    Fourier Features Let Networks Learn High Frequency Functions in Low Dimensional
    Domains (Fourier condition bands in the adapter)
        Tancik, Srinivasan, Mildenhall, Fridovich-Keil, Raghavan,
        Singhal, Ramamoorthi, Barron, Ng.                      arXiv:2006.10739
    Classifier-free graph diffusion for molecular property targeting (FreeGress; the
    node-count conditioning idea and the property-targeting evaluation protocol)
        Ninniri, Podda, Bacciu.                                arXiv:2312.17397

The implementations here are independent adaptations to DeFoG's categorical outputs, not the
authors' code. Any error in them is this package's.
